<%- include('../partials/head') %>
<%- include('../partials/header') %>
<main id="main"><div class="shell"><section class="section">
  <h1 class="section__title">What this replica does not reproduce</h1>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>This page is generated from <code>analysis/replication_gaps.json</code>. It is the
    deliberate record of what was not accessible or not reproduced &mdash; nothing here is
    papered over elsewhere in the project.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="data">
      <caption><%= gapTotal %> item(s) across <%= Object.keys(gapCounts).length %> categories.</caption>
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">Kind</th><th scope="col" class="num">Count</th><th scope="col">What it means</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <% Object.keys(gapCounts).forEach(function (k) { %>
          <tr><th scope="row"><code><%= k %></code></th>
              <td class="num"><%= gapCounts[k] %></td>
              <td><%= gapMeanings[k] || '—' %></td></tr>
        <% }); %>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <div class="prose">
    <h3>Always out of scope</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Anything behind a login. Authenticated areas were never accessed.</li>
      <li>Anything behind a CAPTCHA. None was reproduced, solved or bypassed; this
      demonstration asks a simple arithmetic question instead.</li>
      <li>The original's database, source code and server behaviour, none of which a public
      frontend exposes.</li>
      <li>The original's success, validation and error states: no form was ever submitted to
      it, so those were never observed and are not guessed at.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section></div></main>
<%- include('../partials/footer') %>
